course: dictionary
lesson: 9791
title: Sushi: a word from Japan
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sushi is a food from Japan. It is made of small pieces of cold rice mixed with vinegar, often with fish, egg or vegetables on top or inside. Sometimes it is wrapped in seaweed.
explain: Use the context to work out what sushi is. «Sushi uses rice with vinegar and fish or vegetables.» The clues are rice, vinegar, fish and vegetables, so sushi is a kind of food, not a sport or a place.
explain: Sushi is usually eaten in small bites, with chopsticks or fingers. People often dip it in soy sauce, and they add a little wasabi, which is a hot green paste, so a little goes a long way.
fact: Sushi is a Japanese food made of small pieces of cold rice with vinegar.
fact: Sushi can have raw or cooked fish, egg or vegetables, and it is sometimes rolled in seaweed.
fact: «Sushi uses rice with vinegar and fish or vegetables.»
fact: Raw fish must be very fresh and kept cold, and sometimes it is frozen first to kill parasites.
fact: Sushi is uncountable, so we say some sushi, not a sushi.
exercise: Where does sushi come from? | Egypt | *Japan | Mexico | Italy
exercise: «Sushi uses rice with vinegar and fish or vegetables.» What is the rice mixed with? | Chocolate | Milk | *Vinegar | Ketchup
exercise: Why must raw fish in sushi be very fresh? | *To keep it safe to eat | To make it taste sweeter | To make it heavier | To turn it green
test: Sushi is usually eaten how? | *In small bites, with chopsticks or fingers | In one huge bowl with a spoon | Frozen solid, like ice lollies | Hot, straight from the oven
test: What is wasabi? | A kind of fish | A type of bread | *A hot green paste | A sweet red sauce
exam: Which sentence about sushi is true? | It is a drink made from tea leaves | It is a sport played on a beach | It is a bread baked in a hot oven | *It is a Japanese food of small rice pieces with vinegar
